## Premises (measured by the feed2 drafter at 22:39:02 AEST, in a `--shared` scratchpad clone detached at 581ed7fa1; Wednesday re-derives before queueing)
- THE CLASSIFIED DEFECT of `KS-1229-R15-UNTYPEDSRC.md` (run `runs/2026-09-21_ks1229-ornith35b-night`, FAIL T5 "Cannot nest a describe inside a test"): the fence was a pure insertion with TRAILING context only (:209-211, the KS-1202 describe's first three lines). The model normalised it into "2 leading + 2 trailing" context and the block landed INSIDE the KS-1202 describe's `create` helper. Rule earned (IMPROVEMENTS 22:22): a new describe's anchor is a line at DESCRIBE level, verified by indentation. This file separates every top-level block with a BLANK line, which a modify fence may not carry, and git apply pins a hunk with NO trailing context to the END of the file - so the anchor is the file's LAST line: the column-0 `});` that closes the KS-1202 describe at :226 is removed and re-emitted with a trailing comment (`}); // KS-1202 create guard`, the file's own closer-comment style) and the new describe follows it at top level, ending the file (the model cannot slide a hunk that carries a '-' line and ends at EOF). Every name the cells use (`write` :128, `ISSUER` :93, `SOURCE_ID` :123, `seed` :124, `REFUSED` :141) is declared above.
- A SECOND DEFECT the classification did not name: the R15 brief's tamper was `certifications.ts:201` (the /api/certifications/issue guard, copied from `night/briefs/KS-1229.md` - the SIDE-EFFECTS row), which the sign-cert cells never reach; it would have failed T6 "reds NOTHING" after the anchor fix. The UNTYPEDSRC tamper is the one in `night/briefs/split_1229untyped/KS-1229.md` and the 09-18 READY: the /sign-cert relabel guard `if (metadata.documentType !== undefined && metadata.documentType !== source.type) {` at documents.ts (old :2590, at the tip :2609; the one-line text occurs 3x - :1993 /version, :2609 /sign-cert, :2878 /sign-wallet - so it is a BLOCK tamper, the same unique 5-line block the held SIGNCERT-R15 sibling uses, with only its first line changed).
- Reachability at 581ed7fa1: U1 seeds an in-memory source with `type: undefined` and POSTs /api/documents/:id/sign-cert with `metadata.documentType: 'DEGREE'`. The handler resolves the source (:2604) and reaches the guard at :2609: at the tip `'DEGREE' !== undefined` is true -> 400 BAD_REQUEST before any upstream call (GREEN, `REFUSED`). Under the tamper the prepended `typeof source.type === 'string' &&` is false for an untyped source -> the guard is skipped, the handler signs and saves -> U1 reads status 201 (RED by assertion at `.toEqual`). The control seeds `'DOCUMENT'` (a string) so the tampered conjunct is true and the guard evaluates exactly as at the tip -> 400 on both trees. Every existing sign-cert cell seeds a string-typed source, so nothing else reds.
- SIBLINGS on this file (feed2 precheck, same clone): AFTERVERIFY anchors at :118-120 (top level, unchanged), VERSIONTRIM re-anchored at :123/124, SIGNWALLET at :141/142, SIGNCERT at :116/117 - four DISTINCT top-level seams (SIGNCERT :116/117, AFTERVERIFY :119/120, VERSIONTRIM :123/124, SIGNWALLET :141/142) plus this one at EOF; the five hunks are disjoint, so the raise seat can apply all five patches in file order at the tip.
- Ticket KS-1229: Backlog; nothing in the product changes; in-memory only (`fromDbRow` gives `type = document_type || 'document'`, so an untyped source is unreachable through Postgres - this pins the handler's own guard).

## What is wrong (one paragraph)
`services/originate/src/routes/documents.ts` refuses a /sign-cert whose `metadata.documentType` differs from the source's stored type (:2609) - KS-1213 closed the relabel. Nothing pins that the refusal ALSO holds when the source row has NO type (`source.type` undefined): a guard that first checked `typeof source.type === 'string'` would skip the refusal, sign and save a relabelled version. The code is RIGHT at the tip. This task is the PIN, test-only: one new top-level describe in the existing ks1213 file whose RED cell reds under that tamper and whose control (a typed source, differing label) is refused on both trees.

## THE MODE - read this twice
TEST-ONLY, MODIFY IN PLACE: your diff contains EXACTLY ONE file, the EXISTING test file above, as the ONE hunk below (context lines byte-for-byte from the tip; no blank context line; no blank + line). No product hunk. The hunk header is `@@ -224,3 +224,15 @@`: two context lines (:224, :225 - the last cell of the KS-1202 describe and its `  });`), one '-' line (the file's LAST line, `});` at :226), then 13 '+' lines: the same closer re-emitted with a trailing comment, then the new describe. Your '+' lines come AFTER the '-' line and there is NO context after them - the hunk ends the file.

